==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To apply mental or physical effort to (something) in order to [[shape]], [[form]], [[improve]], [[investigate]], [[solve]] it, etc.
#: {{ux|en|John's in the studio '''working on''' the plans for the new house.}}
#: {{ux|en|I've been '''working on''' this problem for several days, but I still haven't figured it out.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[exercise]] [[influence]] on someone.
#: {{ux|en|Leave it to me. I'll try to '''work on''' the boss to give us the day off.}}
# {{&lit|en|work|on}}
#: ''Do you work on Sundays?''
